<LessonLayout title="Catechist's Guide &mdash; Sin" cic="CCC 1846-1876" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For preparing and leading the class.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated time:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Core topic:</strong> Sin is real and breaks our relationship with God and others, but God&rsquo;s mercy is always greater.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Define sin as an act of unloving that wounds our relationship with God.</li>
<li>Distinguish between mortal and venial sin.</li>
<li>Recognize the capital vices as roots of sin.</li>
<li>Convey trust in divine mercy as the central message.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;Where sin abounded, grace abounded all the more&raquo; (Rom 5:20)</p>
<p><strong>Catechism references:</strong> CCC 1846-1876</p>

</section>

